<title>USA: Data Documents Inc Q1 net up, sales fall.</title>
<headline>Data Documents Inc Q1 net up, sales fall.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, NE 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997	1996</p>
<p> NET SALES					 $  62,583  $  65,040</p>
<p> COST OF GOODS SOLD				 45,727     48,721</p>
<p>     Gross Profit				   16,856     16,319</p>
<p> SELLING, GENERAL, ADMINISTRATIVE EXPENSES   9,785	9,499</p>
<p>     Operating Income				7,071	6,820</p>
<p>DEBT EXPENSE, net, including amortization of</p>
<p>   $201,000 and $208,000			   2,353	2,520</p>
<p> INCOME BEFORE INCOME TAXES			4,718	4,300</p>
<p> INCOME TAX EXPENSE				  1,913	1,745</p>
<p> NET INCOME					    2,805	2,555</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER COMMON SHARE:</p>
<p>     Primary					    0.28	 0.26</p>
<p> AVERAGE SHARES OUTSTANDING:		     9,958	9,904</p>
<p>(Columnar Amounts in Thousands, Except Share, Per Share Data)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 Q1 sales were in line with expectations, and reflect effects of a 6.1 percent decrease in paper prices, which are passed on to customers when they occur, and by the continued, planned reduction in sales of stock forms. Stock form sales decreased by 29.1 percent for the quarter.</p>
<p>		   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
